@page "/"

<PageTitle>FaFa Showcase</PageTitle>

<h1>FaFa Showcase</h1>
<p class="fa-mb-4">
    A live, in-repo demo of the <code>Blazor/</code> style library — every component,
    rendered for real, with the actual markup used to produce it. One page per
    component, grouped the same way as
    <a href="https://github.com/parrescence/FaFa/blob/dev/Blazor/docs/index.md" target="_blank">Blazor/docs/index.md</a>.
    This app isn't published anywhere yet; you're looking at it by pulling this
    branch and running it locally (see <code>Showcase/README.md</code>).
</p>

<FaCard CssClass="fa-mb-4">
    <h3>How this app is wired up</h3>
    <p>
        This client references <code>Blazor/FaFa.csproj</code> directly via
        <code>&lt;ProjectReference&gt;</code> — not the published GitHub Packages
        package — so it always shows whatever's currently on this branch, including
        in-progress work. A real consumer app outside this repo installs the package
        instead; see <a href="https://github.com/parrescence/FaFa/blob/dev/Blazor/docs/install.md" target="_blank">Blazor/docs/install.md</a>
        for that path.
    </p>
    <p>
        <code>Showcase.Web.Api</code> is a small local-only API (in-memory sample
        data, no auth, no database) that backs the "pulled from the database" demos —
        <code>FaGrid</code>'s <code>ItemsProvider</code>, <code>FaCarousel</code>'s
        <code>ItemsProvider</code>, and <code>FaLoginForm</code>'s <code>OnSubmit</code>.
        Everything else on these pages runs entirely client-side.
    </p>
</FaCard>

<h2>Buttons &amp; feedback</h2>
<ul class="fa-mb-4">
    <li><a href="/fa-button">Buttons</a> <code>FaButton</code> — the standard button/link, 7 color variants</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-card">Cards</a> <code>FaCard</code> — bordered, optionally clickable tile</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-alert">Alerts</a> <code>FaAlert</code> — info/success/danger banner</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-badge">Badges</a> <code>FaBadge</code> — small pill label</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-avatar">Avatars</a> <code>FaAvatar</code> — photo or initials circle</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-modal">Modals</a> <code>FaModal</code> — backdrop dialog, caller owns open/closed state</li>
</ul>

<h2>Form fields</h2>
<ul class="fa-mb-4">
    <li><a href="/fa-input">Text Input</a> <code>FaInput</code> — generic text/number field</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-select">Select</a> <code>FaSelect</code> — plain <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>, options as child content</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-search-select">Search Select</a> <code>FaSearchSelect</code> — type-to-search combobox over your own query function</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-dropdown">Dropdown</a> <code>FaDropdown</code> — type-to-filter combobox over a local list, windowed to N visible rows</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-textarea">Textarea</a> <code>FaTextarea</code> — multi-line text, optional maxlength counter</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-checkbox">Checkbox</a> <code>FaCheckbox</code> — checkbox with a clickable label</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-radio-group">Radio Group</a> <code>FaRadioGroup</code> — a group of radio buttons from a tuple list</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-toggle">Toggle</a> <code>FaToggle</code> — segmented N-option switch, with an optional companion input</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-date-picker">Date Picker</a> <code>FaDatePicker</code> — day/month/year fields + calendar popup</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-date-range">Date Range</a> <code>FaDateRange</code> — linked From/To date fields</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-currency">Currency Input</a> <code>FaCurrency</code> — formatted amount field</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-file">File Upload</a> <code>FaFile</code> — file picker, optionally styled as a button</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data display</h2>
<ul class="fa-mb-4">
    <li><a href="/fa-table">Table</a> <code>FaTable</code> — plain typed <code>&lt;table&gt;</code>, you own paging/filtering</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-grid">Data Grid</a> <code>FaGrid</code> — a table with its own paging/rows-per-page/sort/filter, in-memory or provider-backed</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-carousel">Carousel</a> <code>FaCarousel</code> — one-slide-at-a-time slideshow, in-memory or provider-backed</li>
</ul>

<h2>Self-contained forms</h2>
<ul class="fa-mb-4">
    <li><a href="/fa-form">Form</a> <code>FaForm</code> — wraps EditForm around your own field markup, returns the populated model on submit</li>
    <li><a href="/fa-login-form">Login Form</a> <code>FaLoginForm</code> — username/password + remember-me, emits an <code>FaLoginRequest</code></li>
    <li><a href="/fa-logout-form">Logout Form</a> <code>FaLogoutForm</code> — "are you sure?" confirm/cancel</li>
</ul>

<h2>Progress &amp; loaders</h2>
<ul class="fa-mb-4">
    <li><a href="/fa-progress">Progress Bar</a> <code>FaProgress</code> — filled track, 4 fill directions</li>
